---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Sofa Cleaning London"
  description="The terms on which Sofa Cleaning London provides upholstery and carpet cleaning, including quotes, access, cancellations and the limits of what cleaning can achieve."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Terms of service"
    lede="What you can expect from us and what we need from you. Written to be read rather than skipped."
    trail={[{ href: '/terms/', label: 'Terms' }]}
  />

  <section class="container-page py-14 md:py-20">
    <article class="prose-body max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="mt-0">Quotes</h2>
      <p>
        Prices shown on this site are starting prices for normally soiled items and are not offers
        in themselves. A quote given from your photograph and description is fixed for that job as
        described.
      </p>
      <p>
        If, on arrival, the job is materially different from what was described — more items, more
        rooms, heavy pet contamination, or a previous cleaning attempt that has to be reversed — we
        will explain the difference and give you a revised price before starting. You are free to
        decline at that point with nothing to pay.
      </p>

      <h2>What cleaning can and cannot do</h2>
      <p>
        We test fabrics before cleaning and will tell you what we expect to achieve. Cleaning
        removes soiling. It does not reverse physical wear, abrasion, fading from sunlight, bleaching,
        cracked or peeling finishes, or dye damage that has bonded to the fibre.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where we believe a mark will only reduce rather than disappear, we will say so before we
        start. Proceeding on that basis means the result is not a failure of the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we consider a fabric cannot be cleaned safely, we will decline the item and explain why.
        There is no charge for a visit that ends this way.
      </p>

      <h2>Access and preparation</h2>
      <p>
        We need reasonable access to the property, an electricity supply, and somewhere to park
        within roughly thirty metres of the entrance. Where parking is controlled, a visitor permit
        or pre-booked bay is the customer's responsibility; any parking charge or road charge that
        applies will be itemised in your quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please clear small items, breakables and floor clutter before we arrive. We move furniture
        that two people can move safely, and we do not move pianos, aquariums, large electronics or
        anything fixed in place.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Let us know as early as you can if you need to cancel or rearrange; there is no charge for
        doing so with reasonable notice. If we arrive at a pre-arranged appointment and cannot gain
        access, a call-out charge may apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment is due on completion unless agreed otherwise in writing. Commercial and letting-agent
        work may be invoiced on agreed terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Problems</h2>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with any part of the work, tell us within 48 hours and we will return to
        look at it. Most issues — a mark that reappears by wicking, an area that dried unevenly — are
        straightforward to put right, and we would much rather do that than leave you dissatisfied.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights as a consumer under UK law.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} — <a href={`tel:${site.phoneE164}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> or
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
